From dc6759151637eef479c18fd00a101b138222e796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 23:28:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] microblaze: use PC-relative encodings for .eh_frame pointers

MicroBlaze is the last Linux target still using DW_EH_PE_aligned for
PIC exception tables.  Absolute pointers in .eh_frame mean that every
shared object carries a writable .eh_frame and a dynamic relocation
per FDE (711 R_MICROBLAZE_REL entries in glibc's libc.so), and that ld
cannot build the .eh_frame_hdr binary search table ("FDE encoding in
... prevents .eh_frame_hdr table being created"), so the unwinder
walks every FDE in an object on each frame.

The reason was purely an assembler limitation: gas for MicroBlaze did
not accept "sym - ." across sections.  binutils 2.46 does, emitting
R_MICROBLAZE_32_PCREL, so use the encodings every other ELF target
uses: pcrel|sdata4 for code pointers, indirect|pcrel|sdata4 for
global (personality) pointers.  With that, .eh_frame links read-only
without dynamic relocations, the .eh_frame_hdr table is built, and
unwinding through a shared object works unchanged (verified with
_Unwind_Backtrace across a DSO on glibc under qemu-user).

Requires binutils with the matching gas/ld change; older assemblers
reject the "sym - ." expressions.

gcc/ChangeLog:
	* config/microblaze/microblaze.h (ASM_PREFERRED_EH_DATA_FORMAT):
	Use DW_EH_PE_pcrel | DW_EH_PE_sdata4, indirect for global
	pointers, instead of DW_EH_PE_aligned.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h b/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h
index fc8c4b871..ce0b7635f 100644
--- a/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h
+++ b/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.h
@@ -205,8 +205,12 @@ extern enum pipeline_type microblaze_pipe;
 /* Select a format to encode pointers in exception handling data.  CODE
    is 0 for data, 1 for code labels, 2 for function pointers.  GLOBAL is
    true if the symbol may be affected by dynamic relocations.  */
+/* PC-relative pointers keep .eh_frame read-only, need no dynamic
+   relocations, and let the linker build the .eh_frame_hdr search table
+   (it refuses to for DW_EH_PE_aligned).  Requires an assembler that
+   accepts "sym - ." across sections (binutils 2.46).  */
 #define ASM_PREFERRED_EH_DATA_FORMAT(CODE,GLOBAL) \
-  ((flag_pic || GLOBAL) ? DW_EH_PE_aligned : DW_EH_PE_absptr)
+  (((GLOBAL) ? DW_EH_PE_indirect : 0) | DW_EH_PE_pcrel | DW_EH_PE_sdata4)
 
 /* Use DWARF 2 debugging information by default.  */
 #define DWARF2_DEBUGGING_INFO
